  "interpretation": "<p>Fluid TLC measures the <strong data-start=\"110\" data-end=\"154\">total number of white blood cells (WBCs)</strong> in a body fluid sample</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Fluid Type</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal TLC</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Significance of Elevation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pleural fluid</strong></td>\n<td>&lt; 1000 cells/&micro;L</td>\n<td>&gt;1000: Infection, TB, malignancy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ascitic fluid</strong></td>\n<td>&lt; 250 cells/&micro;L</td>\n<td>&ge;250: <strong>Spontaneous Bacterial Peritonitis (SBP)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pericardial fluid</strong></td>\n<td>&lt; 1000 cells/&micro;L</td>\n<td>Elevated: Infection, autoimmune disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>CSF</strong></td>\n<td>0&ndash;5 cells/&micro;L (mostly lymphocytes)</td>\n<td>Elevated: Meningitis (bacterial, viral, TB), malignancy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Synovial fluid</strong></td>\n<td>&lt; 200 cells/&micro;L</td>\n<td>200&ndash;2000: Non-inflammatory; &gt;2000: Inflammatory or septic arthritis</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>TLC Range</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Likely Cause</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong></td>\n<td>Transudative fluid (CHF, cirrhosis, nephrotic syndrome)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Mildly Elevated (500&ndash;1000)</strong></td>\n<td>Early infection, TB, malignancy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Markedly Elevated (&gt;1000)</strong></td>\n<td>Bacterial infection, empyema, severe inflammation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Extremely High (&gt;10,000)</strong></td>\n<td>Often suggests <strong>purulent bacterial infection</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
